## Integrated Local Runtime

The stage-local implementations can now be composed as one receipt-preserving
run. An optional final stage compiles promotion decisions into no-side-effect
Shadow Execution Plans and Action Receipts.

```text
Observation
→ Ingest
→ Proxy
→ Protocol Candidate
→ Simulation
→ Selection
→ PoC Promotion
→ Shadow Execution Plan
→ Action Receipt
```

```bash
python -m src.foundry \
  examples/idea_observations/input.jsonl \
  --output-dir receipts/full_run \
  --scenario-count 30 \
  --current-level 2 \
  --next-level 3 \
  --shadow-bindings examples/full_run/adapter_bindings.yaml \
  --execution-inputs examples/full_run/execution_inputs.yaml
```

A blocked result is a valid result. Generated candidates begin unconfirmed, and
unknown evidence, insufficient promotion, missing inputs, pending approvals,
or missing adapter bindings remain outside the execution boundary. Shadow mode
never invokes an adapter and records `external_effects: []`.

See `docs/local-runtime.md` for the complete contract and artifact list.
